  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Why does this happen",
      "char_file": "커피_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "A loose muscle between your",
        "stomach and esophagus",
        "",
        "lets stomach acid",
        "push back up"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Coffee",
      "char_file": "커피_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Caffeine relaxes that muscle",
        "and boosts acid production",
        "",
        "Worse on an empty stomach"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Coffee — how to fix it",
      "char_file": "커피_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Have it with a meal, and cut off",
        "a few hours before bed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Spicy food",
      "char_file": "고추_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Nearly half of reflux sufferers",
        "say spicy food makes it worse",
        "",
        "Capsaicin irritates the esophagus",
        "going down, and slows digestion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Spicy food — try this instead",
      "char_file": "고추_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Cut hot sauce to a small drizzle,",
        "or season with basil or oregano"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Tomato sauce",
      "char_file": "토마토_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Pizza, pasta, ketchup —",
        "tomatoes are naturally acidic",
        "",
        "About 1 in 10 reflux sufferers",
        "point to tomato dishes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Tomato sauce — try this instead",
      "char_file": "토마토_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "A pinch of baking soda in the sauce",
        "neutralizes a good chunk of the acid",
        "",
        "Before it ever hits your stomach"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "closing": {
    "headline": [
      ["None of these need to", "disappear completely"],
      ["Just watch the timing", "and the portions"]
    ],
    "tip": [
      "Pay attention to what your body",
      "tells you after each meal"
    ],
